<title>NIGERIA: Shell Nigeria says workers' pay dispute resolved.</title>
<headline>Shell Nigeria says workers' pay dispute resolved.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch Shell's Nigerian unit said on Wednesday a dispute with its workers over pay had been resolved without any disruption to its operations.</p>
<p>&quot;A minor problem over remuneration made a mix of some junior and senior workers go on strike on Monday,&quot; a senior official of the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;The dispute was resolved the same day without any disruption to operations including crude oil liftings. Everything has been normal,&quot; the company official added.</p>
<p>Shell, one of six multinationals operating in Nigeria, pumps about half the country's nearly two million barrels per day of crude oil.</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17</p>
</text>
